# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The package description for tools/package.py (NBTFoundry/manager): one argument
# per line. `make package` and the release workflow both use it; they add the
# version, sequence, key, output and executable. Bridge 1.6: an ordinary QNX
# program built with the NBT toolchain (no runner); it draws on the manager's
# surface (show) and turns pages with the controller. Optional: iDrive's car
# data (the names src/sources.cpp reads, in that order), definition files
# (`files`: CSV, README "Definition files"), live settings and a status line.
--app
gauges
--compat
nbt_6.5_armv7
--bridge
1.6
--bridge-uses
show,controller
--bridge-optional
status,live-settings,car-data,files
--bridge-cds
engine.RPMSpeed,engine.temperature,engine.torque,driving.acceleratorPedal,driving.speedActual,sensors.temperatureExterior,driving.acceleration,driving.steeringWheel,driving.gear,driving.mode
--bridge-files
csv|1|4
--setting
source|Data source|auto|auto,dme,cardata,demo
--setting
units|Units|metric|metric,imperial
--setting
lambda|Lambda as|lambda|lambda,afr
--setting
boost_scale|Boost gauge top|2bar|1bar,1-5bar,2bar,2-5bar,3bar
--setting
drivetrain|Drivetrain|auto|auto,rwd,xdrive
--setting
debug_log|Debug log|off|off,on
# What the phone app shows before an install (NBT Manager's PROTOCOL.md,
# "Package information").
--property
Project|NBTFoundry nf-gauges
--property
Licence|MPL-2.0; LVGL MIT; Montserrat OFL-1.1
--text
Live engine gauges: boost, lambda, ignition timing and per-cylinder corrections, fuel pressure, temperatures.
--text
On a diesel, the particulate filter. The transmission: gear, wheel speeds and slip, drivetrain, torque and power curves.
--text
Reads the engine computer (DME) through the car's gateway, read-only, as a diagnostic tester does.
--text
iDrive's own car data fills in what the DME does not give.
--text=
--text
Do not interact with it while driving.
--text=
--text
